From: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt7993: stop the patch semaphore release from spinning forever

When the endpoint leaves the bus right after PATCH_FINISH_REQ,
mcu_wm_patch_sem_ctrl(dev, 0) cannot reach the chip either, so it returns -110
and the default arm jumps back to the out: label - which retries the very same
failing write.  The loop never ends, it holds rtnl for the whole time, and the
only way out is cutting power: sysrq is not enabled on this image and the
watchdog is not armed, so the last few hardware attempts had to be power
cycled instead of rebooted.

Log the error code and fall through.  The semaphore is gone either way, and
the caller needs to see the failure rather than a console that repeats the
same line every twenty seconds until the board is unplugged.

Signed-off-by: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
---
--- a/wlan_hwifi/mcu/mcu_wm.c
+++ b/wlan_hwifi/mcu/mcu_wm.c
@@ -378,8 +378,8 @@
 		break;
 	default:
 		ret = -EAGAIN;
-		dev_err(dev->dev, "Failed to release patch semaphore\n");
-		goto out;
+		dev_err(dev->dev,
+			"Failed to release patch semaphore, sem=%d\n", sem);
 	}
 	if (mcu_entry->applied_method == BIN_METHOD)
 		release_firmware(fw);
